# RETIRED SCAFFOLD SOURCE (SN-028). This dial now lives in
# process.toml.template -> docs/process.toml as `[policies] review_rounds`, and
# bootstrap.py no longer copies this file into a new repo — shipping both
# homes would hand every scaffold the mixed-config refusal. The file stays
# in the kit as the reference for the legacy vocabulary that
# `bootstrap.py --migrate-config` reads when converting an existing
# adoption; the text below describes that legacy home, not today's.
#
# Review policy (process-options.md "Unattended operation" — the reviewer
# dial). One value on the last line — how many independent fresh-context
# review verdicts a completed work item gets before the integrator accepts it:
#   0 — no mechanized review leg (harness gates only).
#   1 — one reviewer session (the default).
#   2 — two reviewers with SPLIT charters (cross-provider recommended).
# The floors above the dial, the A/B charter split, and how sessions are
# dispatched (the REVIEW-A/REVIEW-B phase convention + AGENT_CMD_MAP) are
# owned by process-options.md "Unattended operation" — stated once there, not
# restated here (the gate-policy / push-policy templates keep the same shape).
1
